---
// The Family Guide — the page someone lands on after enrolling, and the one
// they come back to later.
//
// Copy is Rob's APPROVED family-guide draft (2026-08-06), so this page is
// indexable. The safety wording mirrors language already approved on /terms and
// remains open for attorney review — docs/legal-source.md §4 item 8 (b).
//
// The disaster paragraph that used to sit beside it is GONE (2026-08-10). It
// was phrased as effort rather than guaranteed arrival, which was the right
// hedge, but we cannot perform the in-person check at all — so the honest move
// was to remove it rather than qualify it further. Item 8 (c) is closed by
// deletion, not by wording.
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT PERSONALIZED. This page is permanent and bookmarkable, so it
// is written to work for someone arriving cold months later. Passing a
// recipient's name through a query string would put a third party's name into
// browser history, shared links and referrer headers to buy a little warmth on
// one visit — the flow's no-third-party-data-in-URLs rule applies here too.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const SUPPORT_EMAIL = 'Mabel@AuntMabel.app';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Your family guide · Aunt Mabel"
  description="Everything you'll want to know about your loved one's daily call from Aunt Mabel."
>
  <div class="wrap guide">
    <header class="guide-head">
      <p class="kicker">You're all set</p>
      <h1>Welcome to the family.</h1>
      <p class="guide-lede">
        Mabel will call your loved one at their chosen time, every day. Below is
        everything worth knowing — how to introduce her, what the calls are
        like, and how to reach us. Keep this page bookmarked; it's here whenever
        you need it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#talking">Talking to them about Mabel</a>
      <a href="#expect">What to expect</a>
      <a href="#safety">Important to know</a>
      <a href="#account">Your account</a>
    </nav>

    {/* ── 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="talking">
      <p class="section-num">One</p>
      <h2>How to talk to them about Aunt Mabel</h2>
      <p>
        A friendly heads-up makes the first call land as a warm surprise instead
        of a strange one. A few gentle suggestions:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Tell them ahead of time.</strong> Let them know a nice call is
          coming so an unknown number isn't a worry. Something simple like:
          <span class="say-this">
            "I signed us up for a friendly check-in call each morning — her
            name's Aunt Mabel. She just wants to say hello and make sure you're
            doing alright."
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Keep it warm, not clinical.</strong> This isn't monitoring —
          it's a daily visit from someone who's glad to hear their voice. Framing
          it as company, not surveillance, helps.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Be honest if they ask.</strong> Mabel is a friendly automated
          helper, and she'll say so kindly if they ask. You can too — most folks
          warm right up once they've talked to her.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>There's no wrong way to talk to her.</strong> They can just
          chat like they would with a neighbor. She loves a good story.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>It's okay to say no.</strong> On the very first call, Mabel
          will ask if the daily calls are welcome. If they'd rather not, that's
          completely fine — the calls stop, and you won't be charged.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    {/* ── 2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="expect">
      <p class="section-num">Two</p>
      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          {/* (281) is Houston, matching the engine's FROM_NUMBER
              (+12816999063 in wrangler.toml). If that number ever changes,
              this sentence has to change with it. */}
          <strong>The first call</strong> comes at their chosen time, from a
          Houston <strong>(281)</strong> number. A heads-up — see above — helps
          most.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The first call is a little special.</strong> Mabel introduces
          herself, mentions the family set this up, and confirms the calls are
          welcome.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>After that:</strong> a warm, short daily visit — she asks how
          they slept, whether they've eaten, how they're feeling, and follows
          wherever the conversation goes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The free trial:</strong> your first 14 days are free. We don't
          charge until your loved one has truly welcomed Mabel into their mornings.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    {/* ── 3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="safety">
      <p class="section-num">Three</p>
      <h2>Important to know</h2>

      <div class="safety-callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Aunt Mabel is a friendly daily check-in — not an emergency,
          medical, or monitoring service.</strong> She is not a substitute for
          911, for a medical alert device, or for professional care.
        </p>
        <p class="safety-emergency">
          In an urgent situation, always call <strong>911</strong> or their
          doctor directly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>Being plain about where the edges are:</p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li><strong>No one is monitored between calls.</strong> Mabel speaks to them once a day. She isn't listening the rest of the time, and she can't detect a fall or a medical event.</li>
        <li><strong>She won't call a doctor.</strong> If you gave us a doctor's details, we pass them along when we alert your contacts. We never call them ourselves.</li>
        <li><strong>She isn't medical advice.</strong> Mabel doesn't diagnose anything or weigh in on medication.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Mabel does do</h3>
      <p>
        If something concerning comes up in a call, we email <strong>you</strong>
        and <strong>the emergency contact you listed</strong>, so a real person
        can follow up. You decide what to do from there — we surface it, you make
        the call.
      </p>

      {/*
        REMOVED 2026-08-10 — "When disaster strikes", promising an in-person
        wellness check by the Cajun Navy Ground Force. Carefully hedged as a
        commitment to TRY rather than a guarantee, but we cannot deliver it at
        all today, and a hedge on a capability that does not exist is still a
        promise. The partnership stays on the site as heritage.
      */}
    </section>

    {/* ── 4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="account">
      <p class="section-num">Four</p>
      <h2>Your account, and how to cancel</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <strong>You're in control.</strong> Pause or cancel anytime — no
          contract, no cancellation fee.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To cancel or get help:</strong> email us at
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Alerts come to you</strong> (your email) and to the emergency
          contact you listed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Adding another loved one:</strong> you can enroll a second
          parent or grandparent anytime — same account, their own daily call.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Cancel anytime, from your account. The calls carry on to the end of the
        period you've already paid for and then stop — nothing is cut off the
        moment you click. If you cancel during the free trial, you're never
        charged at all.
      </p>

      <div class="contact-card-guide">
        <p class="contact-label">Talk to a person</p>
        <p class="contact-email">
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
        </p>
        <p class="contact-note">
          A real human reads these. If something's wrong with a call, say so —
          it's the fastest way to get it fixed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="guide-foot">
      Aunt Mabel is operated by Trustlight LLC. She was born from years of
      disaster response with the Cajun Navy Ground Force — where the same thing
      turned up after every storm: elderly people, alone.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide { max-width: 44rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; }

  .guide-head { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .guide-head h1 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .guide-lede {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--soft-ink);
    max-width: 40ch;
  }

  /* Quiet jump links — this page is long and people come back to it looking
     for one specific thing. */
  .guide-toc {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .guide-toc a {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--rose-deep);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .guide-toc a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--rose); }

  .guide-section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; scroll-margin-top: 2rem; }
  .section-num {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--rose);
  }
  .guide-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 1.95rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .guide-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.22rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .guide-section p {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.72;
    font-weight: 300;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .guide-section strong { font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }

  .guide-list { margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .guide-list li {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .guide-list a { color: var(--rose-deep); }

  /* The suggested line to actually say out loud — set apart so it reads as
     something to borrow rather than more prose to wade through. */
  .say-this {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--rose);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* Rose, not gold: this is the one part of the page that must read as a
     limit rather than a feature. */
  .safety-callout {
    padding: 22px 26px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rose);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--rose);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .safety-callout p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .safety-emergency {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--rose-deep);
  }
  .safety-emergency strong { color: var(--rose-deep); font-weight: 600; }

  .honest-note {
    padding: 18px 22px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .contact-card-guide {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 20px;
  }
  .contact-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem !important;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--soft-ink);
  }
  .contact-email {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem !important;
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .contact-email a { color: var(--rose-deep); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rose); }
  .contact-note { margin: 0 !important; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--soft-ink); }

  .guide-foot {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--soft-ink);
  }
</style>
